<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The MPC submission dialog (ADR-080): sending a report is never silent. It
  asks for the acknowledgement email, the acknowledgement text, the target and
  the mode (Normal or Test), shows the server's own answer in the log, and
  refuses to send when the report cannot be built (no email, no header). The
  Astrometry tab owns the behaviour; the dialog stays a dumb container.
  Loaded by gui/mpc_send_dialog.py through gui/ui_loader.py.
-->
<ui version="4.0">
 <class>MpcSendDialog</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="MpcSendDialog">
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="vbox_send">
   <property name="leftMargin"><number>11</number></property>
   <property name="topMargin"><number>11</number></property>
   <property name="rightMargin"><number>11</number></property>
   <property name="bottomMargin"><number>11</number></property>
   <item><widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_intro"><property name="text"><string/></property><property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property><property name="toolTip"><string>What the batch about to be sent carries: how many observations, the format, the target and the mode. It is read from the report the moment the window opens, and it follows the target and the mode if you change them here</string></property></widget></item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="txt_log">
     <property name="minimumSize"><size><width>560</width><height>140</height></size></property>
     <property name="readOnly"><bool>true</bool></property>
     <property name="placeholderText"><string>Here the MPC's own answer will appear (the CurlID or the errors) once you press Send.</string></property>
     <property name="font"><font><family>Monospace</family></font></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="row_ack_email">
     <item><widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_ack_email"><property name="text"><string>Ack. email:</string></property><property name="minimumSize"><size><width>90</width><height>0</height></size></property></widget></item>
     <item><widget class="QLineEdit" name="edt_ack_email"><property name="placeholderText"><string>you@example.org</string></property><property name="toolTip"><string>Where the MPC sends its acknowledgement and any designations. It is the contact email you set in Settings, and you can change it here; without it the send is blocked, because the MPC needs it</string></property></widget></item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item>
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="row_ack">
     <item><widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_ack"><property name="text"><string>Ack.:</string></property><property name="minimumSize"><size><width>90</width><height>0</height></size></property></widget></item>
     <item><widget class="QLineEdit" name="edt_ack"><property name="placeholderText"><string>a short acknowledgement text (optional)</string></property><property name="toolTip"><string>A short text the MPC echoes back, so you can tell one batch from another; may stay empty</string></property></widget></item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item>
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="row_target">
     <item><widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_target"><property name="text"><string>Target:</string></property><property name="minimumSize"><size><width>90</width><height>0</height></size></property></widget></item>
     <item><widget class="QComboBox" name="cmb_target"><property name="toolTip"><string>How the MPC routes the batch. Unclassified: the object is already classified (a definitive designation), a normal submission. NEOCP or PCCP: it is on a confirmation page right now. NEW NEO, NEW COMET, NEW NATURAL SATELLITE, NEW TNO, NEW KBO, NEW DISTANT, NEW CENTAUR: a new candidate of that kind. A missing or wrong keyword can misroute the batch or stop it being processed as you expect. The keyword rides the report's ACK line (80 columns) or the obj_type field (ADES)</string></property></widget></item>
     <item><widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_mode"><property name="text"><string>Mode:</string></property></widget></item>
     <item><widget class="QComboBox" name="cmb_mode"><property name="toolTip"><string>Normal sends the batch to the MPC for real: it is processed and published. Test uses the MPC's test endpoint, which runs the same format and validity checks but does NOT process the batch: the rehearsal, to check the report without committing it</string></property></widget></item>
     <item>
      <spacer name="hsp_target">
       <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
       <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>40</width><height>20</height></size></property>
      </spacer>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item><widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_missing"><property name="text"><string/></property><property name="wordWrap"><bool>true</bool></property><property name="styleSheet"><string notr="true">color: #c0392b;</string></property></widget></item>
   <item>
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="row_send">
     <item>
      <spacer name="hsp_send">
       <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
       <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>40</width><height>20</height></size></property>
      </spacer>
     </item>
     <item><widget class="QPushButton" name="btn_send"><property name="text"><string>Send</string></property></widget></item>
     <item><widget class="QPushButton" name="btn_close"><property name="text"><string>Close</string></property></widget></item>
    </layout>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
 <resources/>
 <connections/>
</ui>
